From 12580ad85ded72121c63723868b17160df62570a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:35:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] android: build proton-cachyos 10 for Android (bionic,
 arm64ec)

Carries GameNative's Android stack for Proton 10, with The412Banner's
bionic fixes, onto CachyOS/wine-cachyos cachyos_10.0_20260426/main
(603c2335): the android/ patch set, android_sysvshm, shm_utils and the
build scripts, which apply the patches at configure time.

The patch set was replayed one patch at a time on this tree and every
patch was regenerated from the result, so each goes in with a plain
git apply in build order:

- 32 applied unchanged; dlls_ntdll_unix_fsync_c and
  dlls_winex11_drv_keyboard_c needed fuzz only (same +/- lines).
- dlls_winex11_drv_window_c and dlls_ntdll_unix_server_c were ported by
  hand; CachyOS changed the surrounding code (window_set_managed()
  signature, set_case_insensitive() on drive_c).
- arm64ec/dlls_ntdll_unix_virtual_c keeps the shm_utils include, the
  userfaultfd guard and the force_anon SD-card fix. Its FEX stats shm
  hunks are dropped because CachyOS already has that code, as are the
  FEX unixlib load-by-name hunks, which GameNative's own Proton 10 does
  not use either.
- Dropped because CachyOS already contains them: loader_wine_inf_in,
  dlls_wdscore_wdscore_spec, dlls_ntdll_loader_c, dlls_ntdll_unix_loader_c
  (x86_64 builtins from aarch64-windows), programs_wineboot_wineboot_c
  (FEX TSC scaling), and the whole test-bylaws/ series: CachyOS carries
  Billy Laws' ARM64EC/FEX commits directly (suspend, wow64, xstate, AVX),
  in newer versions than the ones those patches backport.

build-step-arm64ec.sh is the Proton 10 GE script with the GE game-fixes
tier and the DirectAudio check removed; it keeps the ntsync-android build
step and the checks that userspace ntsync is compiled in.

